      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess we need to decide on a single way of passing bit fields.\nEither:\n```\n@Backing(type\u003d\"byte\")\nenum A {\n  a1 \u003d 0x01,\n  a2 \u003d 0x02,\n  a3 \u003d 0x04,\n}\nA[] bitfieldA;\n```\n\nor:\n```\nparcelable B {\n  boolean b1;\n  boolean b2;\n  boolean b3;\n}\nB bitfieldB;\n```\n\nIf we would like to pass only a single bit (let\u0027s say 0x01), solution `A` takes 1 byte, solution `B` takes 12 bytes.\n\nSolution `B` is not scallable as for Audio ChannelAllocation it would always use 116 bytes (4 bytes per bit defined), while `A` just 4 bytes (4 bytes per bit used).",
