        "id": 1928988
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-13T11:37:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s the opaque part of the metadata that we get from the remote device. The BT stack does not understand or interpret it, and just passes it over the AIDL to the vendor module who might be integrating a particular vendor codec and understands the format of this byte array. It can contain a valuable vendor specific data needed by the vendor module to decide on the Codec or QoS configuration that the BT stack gets back from the vendor module. The configuration that the BT stack got from the vendor module is then applied to the remote device endpoint and it can also have this VendorSpecific metadata. But again the BT stack would not understand or interpret this data, just verify the max length defined by the Bluetooth specification and pass it between the remote and the vendor module.",
      "parentUuid": "c1508209_c3549347",
